## Cambio 2 — Función `BuildUpdatedSeriesFormula` completa

**Ctrl+F, buscar el inicio:** `Private Function BuildUpdatedSeriesFormula` y seleccionar hasta el `End Function` que le sigue. Reemplazar todo ese bloque por:

```vba
Private Function BuildUpdatedSeriesFormula(ByVal originalFormula As String, ByVal dataWs As Worksheet) As String

    On Error GoTo Fallback

    Dim firstParen As Long
    Dim innerContent As String
    Dim args As Variant
    Dim ub As Long
    Dim extendBy As Long

    If Left$(originalFormula, 1) <> "=" Then GoTo Fallback
    If Right$(originalFormula, 1) <> ")" Then GoTo Fallback

    firstParen = InStr(originalFormula, "(")
    If firstParen = 0 Then GoTo Fallback

    innerContent = Mid$(originalFormula, firstParen + 1, Len(originalFormula) - firstParen - 1)

    args = SplitTopLevelArgs(innerContent)
    ub = UBound(args)

    If ub < 3 Then GoTo Fallback

    ' El avance se calcula UNA sola vez en base a los VALORES reales
    ' (no nulos, no error) y se aplica igual a categorias y valores
    ' para que ambos rangos queden alineados en la misma columna final.
    extendBy = DetermineExtendBy(CStr(args(2)), dataWs)

    If extendBy <= 0 Then GoTo Fallback

    args(1) = ProcessCatValArg(CStr(args(1)), extendBy)
    args(2) = ProcessCatValArg(CStr(args(2)), extendBy)
    If ub >= 4 Then
        args(4) = ProcessCatValArg(CStr(args(4)), extendBy)
    End If

    BuildUpdatedSeriesFormula = "=SERIES(" & JoinVariant(args) & ")"
    Exit Function

Fallback:
    BuildUpdatedSeriesFormula = originalFormula

End Function
```

## Cambio 3 — Función `ProcessCatValArg` completa

**Ctrl+F, buscar:** `Private Function ProcessCatValArg` hasta su `End Function`. Reemplazar por:

```vba
Private Function ProcessCatValArg(ByVal argStr As String, ByVal extendBy As Long) As String

    Dim trimmed As String
    trimmed = Trim$(argStr)

    If Len(trimmed) = 0 Then
        ProcessCatValArg = argStr
        Exit Function
    End If

    If Left$(trimmed, 1) = "(" And Right$(trimmed, 1) = ")" Then
        Dim inner As String
        Dim parts() As String
        Dim i As Long
        inner = Mid$(trimmed, 2, Len(trimmed) - 2)
        parts = Split(inner, ",")
        For i = LBound(parts) To UBound(parts)
            parts(i) = ProcessArea(Trim$(parts(i)), extendBy)
        Next i
        ProcessCatValArg = "(" & Join(parts, ",") & ")"
    Else
        ProcessCatValArg = ProcessArea(trimmed, extendBy)
    End If

End Function
```

## Cambio 4 — Función `ProcessArea` completa

**Ctrl+F, buscar:** `Private Function ProcessArea` hasta su `End Function`. Reemplazar por (único cambio real: firma con `extendBy` y la línea `newEndCol =`):

```vba
Private Function ProcessArea(ByVal areaStr As String, ByVal extendBy As Long) As String

    On Error GoTo Fallback

    Dim bangPos As Long
    Dim sheetPart As String
    Dim rangePart As String
    Dim startCell As String
    Dim endCell As String
    Dim startCol As String, endCol As String
    Dim startRow As Long, endRow As Long
    Dim newEndCol As String

    bangPos = InStr(areaStr, "!")
    If bangPos = 0 Then GoTo Fallback

    sheetPart = Left$(areaStr, bangPos)
    rangePart = Mid$(areaStr, bangPos + 1)

    If InStr(rangePart, ":") > 0 Then
        startCell = Split(rangePart, ":")(0)
        endCell = Split(rangePart, ":")(1)
    Else
        startCell = rangePart
        endCell = rangePart
    End If

    ParseCellRef startCell, startCol, startRow
    ParseCellRef endCell, endCol, endRow

    If Len(startCol) = 0 Or Len(endCol) = 0 Then GoTo Fallback

    If endRow > startRow And UCase$(endCol) = UCase$(startCol) Then
        ProcessArea = areaStr
        Exit Function
    End If

    newEndCol = ColLettersFromNumber(ColNumberFromLetters(endCol) + extendBy)

    If startCell = endCell Then
        ProcessArea = sheetPart & "$" & newEndCol & "$" & endRow
    Else
        ProcessArea = sheetPart & "$" & startCol & "$" & startRow & ":$" & newEndCol & "$" & endRow
    End If

    Exit Function

Fallback:
    ProcessArea = areaStr

End Function
```

## Cambio 5 — Función nueva `DetermineExtendBy` (agregar, no reemplaza nada)

**Ctrl+F, buscar:**
```
'==================================================================
' Separa los argumentos de nivel superior de SERIES(...) respetando
```
Ese es el comentario justo **antes** de `SplitTopLevelArgs`. Colocá el cursor al **inicio de esa línea** y pegá este bloque completo delante (antes) de ella:

```vba
'==================================================================
' Calcula cuantas columnas hacia la derecha se puede avanzar,
' revisando la fila de VALORES real contra "Data Graf": se detiene
' en la primera celda vacia o con error (#N/A, #DIV/0!, etc).
' Si la primera columna siguiente ya es invalida, retorna 0.
'==================================================================
Private Function DetermineExtendBy(ByVal valArgStr As String, ByVal dataWs As Worksheet) As Long

    On Error GoTo Fallback

    Dim trimmed As String
    Dim lastArea As String
    Dim parts() As String

    trimmed = Trim$(valArgStr)

    If Left$(trimmed, 1) = "(" And Right$(trimmed, 1) = ")" Then
        Dim inner As String
        inner = Mid$(trimmed, 2, Len(trimmed) - 2)
        parts = Split(inner, ",")
        lastArea = Trim$(parts(UBound(parts)))
    Else
        lastArea = trimmed
    End If

    Dim bangPos As Long
    Dim rangePart As String
    Dim endCell As String
    Dim endCol As String
    Dim endRow As Long

    bangPos = InStr(lastArea, "!")
    If bangPos = 0 Then GoTo Fallback
    rangePart = Mid$(lastArea, bangPos + 1)

    If InStr(rangePart, ":") > 0 Then
        endCell = Split(rangePart, ":")(1)
    Else
        endCell = rangePart
    End If

    ParseCellRef endCell, endCol, endRow
    If Len(endCol) = 0 Then GoTo Fallback

    ' No avanzar sobre el patron serie-por-columna (categorias en filas)
    If InStr(rangePart, ":") > 0 Then
        Dim startCell As String, startCol As String, startRow As Long
        startCell = Split(rangePart, ":")(0)
        ParseCellRef startCell, startCol, startRow
        If endRow > startRow And UCase$(endCol) = UCase$(startCol) Then
            DetermineExtendBy = 0
            Exit Function
        End If
    End If

    Dim colNum As Long
    Dim cnt As Long
    Dim v As Variant

    colNum = ColNumberFromLetters(endCol) + 1
    cnt = 0

    Do While colNum <= dataWs.Columns.Count
        v = dataWs.Cells(endRow, colNum).Value
        If IsError(v) Then Exit Do
        If IsEmpty(v) Then Exit Do
        If VarType(v) = vbString Then
            If Len(v) = 0 Then Exit Do
        End If
        cnt = cnt + 1
        colNum = colNum + 1
    Loop

    DetermineExtendBy = cnt
    Exit Function

Fallback:
    DetermineExtendBy = 0

End Function

</parameter>
```

Con esto: si la próxima columna ya es inválida, `extendBy=0` y la serie no se toca; si hay varias columnas válidas seguidas, avanza hasta la última válida en una sola corrida (ya no hace falta ejecutar el macro varias veces). Todo lo demás (rollback, log en Inmediato, charts 15/16/17 sin tocar) sigue igual.
